==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|zickīn||female kid|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*tikk-īn-}} (compare Old English {{term|ticcen||kid|lang=ang}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*digós||goat}}, genitive of {{m|ine-pro|*díks}}. More at {{l|de|Ziege}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Zicken}}
# [[she-goat]], [[nanny goat]]
# a [[touchy]], [[fractious]] or [[difficult]] person (usually, but not necessarily, [[female]])

